[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buster14a/buster/pulls/557","id":5032939616,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVL8Ifc8AAAABK_yQYA","html_url":"https://github.com/buster14a/buster/pull/557","diff_url":"https://github.com/buster14a/buster/pull/557.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/buster14a/buster/pull/557.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buster14a/buster/issues/557","number":557,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"CI: stage trusted conflict and priority admission for the 9700X","user":{"login":"davidgmbb","id":39247043,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjQ3MDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39247043?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb","html_url":"https://github.com/davidgmbb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidgmbb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Advancing a PR base can leave conflicting or obsolete qualification waiting for the shared 9700X, and approvals currently do not change admission order. Add a reviewed-default-branch metadata controller, trusted revision-aware priority/hold/retry controls, and one durable admission lease ahead of the physical queue.\n\nThe existing required context and GitHub Actions integration are retained. PR results are published on the PR head only after a read-only default-branch executor qualifies the pinned current head/base/merge. A same-name commit status keeps a fork-controlled hosted check name from replacing the controller's pending/failing result. Docs-only behavior, benchmark selection, per-PR stale-run cancellation, timeouts and the host lock remain.\n\nThe live runner group serves both Buster and buster-legacy with all-workflow access. A root-owned, initially inert Buster-only job-start wrapper therefore enforces the reviewed default executor before the original lock hook; it preserves legacy access and delegates the original holder/cleanup unchanged. The installed runner is 2.338.0; its default-context export and hook handler were checked against that exact source version. No runner-group access, runner registration or host marker has been changed yet.\n\nValidation: 183 deterministic parser/policy/controller/guard/API-recovery/source-gate checks passed with GCC and with Clang AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer; the updated selector passed 986 checks; actionlint 1.7.12 passed with the existing custom runner labels, and the hook passed Bash syntax validation. The workflow-run reader supports bare and ref-qualified API paths with verified workflow IDs; the real read-only adapter accepted actual PR and main runs. No external implementation or fixture corpus is imported; official actions are pinned.\n\nActivation is deliberately off (`CI_9700X_ADMISSION_ENABLED`). Installing/enabling the reviewed host gate, live required-check/fork attribution, conflict/resolve/promotion/hold/retry/main tests and real 9700X before/after scheduling evidence remain rollout gates, not claimed passes. Operator protocol and the versioned receipts/interface are in docs/ci-9700x-admission.md.\n\nRefs #546, #547, #548. These issues remain open until live acceptance is complete.","created_at":"2026-10-27T11:13:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T11:47:19Z","closed_at":"2026-10-27T11:47:19Z","merged_at":"2026-10-27T11:47:19Z","merge_commit_sha":"78ec3f8a8716cd0a8427caa621acc13c33847135","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers"